Backport of nim-lang/Nim#25855 (fixes #25851) onto the 2.2.10 source tree.

The regression (#25851): under --exceptions:goto + --panics:on the compiler drops
the nimErr_ check after an indirect/closure call whose result flows straight into
another call (`result.add elem(src)`), swallowing a raise and eventually
overflowing the nimInErrorMode bool into a fatal OverflowDefect.

canRaise() in compiler/ast.nim is byte-identical between v2.2.10 and the pre-fix
devel tree, so the upstream one-expression fix applies unchanged: treat a nil
exceptionEffects slot as "effects unknown -> can raise". Applied before `koch
boot`, which recompiles the compiler from source. Upstream fix not yet released in
any 2.2.x tarball; drop this patch once a 2.2.x that contains #25855 ships.

--- a/compiler/ast.nim
+++ b/compiler/ast.nim
@@ -2122,9 +2122,12 @@
     if fn.typ.n[0].kind == nkSym:
       result = false
     else:
+      # Backport of nim-lang/Nim#25855 (fixes #25851): a nil exceptionEffects
+      # slot means "effects unknown", so codegen must assume the call can raise
+      # and keep the nimErr_ check after indirect/closure calls under --panics:on.
       result = ((fn.typ.n[0].len < effectListLen) or
-        (fn.typ.n[0][exceptionEffects] != nil and
-        fn.typ.n[0][exceptionEffects].safeLen > 0))
+        fn.typ.n[0][exceptionEffects] == nil or
+        fn.typ.n[0][exceptionEffects].safeLen > 0)
   else:
     result = false
 
